sdk/python/traceex/tropic.py (step graphs, tropical prefix/suffix values, frontier choice, prefix-suffix composition
with replay and verification, and the basis of verified paths for maximum-likelihood training), node/composition.py,
and examples/tropical_composition (whose countdown.py ports TROPIC's Countdown generator and step environment) are
adapted from TROPIC, the reference code of "Tropical Reinforcement Learning" by Arip Asadulaev, Aladin Djuhera, Karim
Salta, Holger Boche, Fakhri Karray and Martin Takac (MBZUAI, TUM), arXiv:2610.02478,
https://github.com/machinestein/Tropical-Reinforcement-Learning (commit 75106338f320a4c093ea7c1fcfc9fcfc6a5acd20),
in particular ragen/tropic/graph.py, ragen/tropic/collector.py, ragen/tropic/batch.py and ragen/env/countdown/. The
changes for traceX are listed at the top of tropic.py and in examples/tropical_composition/NOTICE. TROPIC is
distributed under the MIT licence, whose notice reads:

